        "orario": "20:21",
        "timestamp": 1774466481,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran rejects US peace plan, issues its own demands Middle East Issued on: 25/03/2026 - 20:21 Iranian state television’s English-language broadcaster quoted an anonymous official as saying Iran rejected America’s ceasefire proposal and has its own demands for an end to the fighting. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran. He explains that the Iranian leadership is \"being emboldened, gaining confidence that they have the upper hand, that they are exacting a cost against Israel and the United States\". Iran media casts doubt on US peace plan as strikes land across the Mideast 25/03/2026 Middle East Israel's defence network challenged by Iranian cluster ballistic missiles 25/03/2026 Middle East Heritage sites in the Middle East under threat due to conflict 25/03/2026 Middle East Iran 'dismisses' US 15-point peace plan, issues its own ceasefire proposal 25/03/2026 Middle East Once seeking de-escalation, Saudi Arabia now sees ‘no coexistence’ with hardline Iran 25/03/2026 Middle East US goals shift: 'At the beginning of the Iran war, the US and Israel were on the same page' 25/03/2026 Middle East US demands of 15-point peace plan likely 'unacceptable' for Iran 25/03/2026 Middle East Unclear 'how much of a negotiation is taking place' between US and Iran 25/03/2026 Middle East What do we know of the US's 15-point peace plan sent to Iran? 25/03/2026 Middle East"
