        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Iran media casts doubt on US peace plan as strikes land across the Mideast Middle East Issued on: 25/03/2026 - 20:17 State media in Iran said Wednesday that Tehran had rejected a US plan to end fighting, as the head of the United Nations warned that the Middle East war was spiralling out of control. In a first public acknowledgement of US efforts to discuss peace, state television cited an unidentified official as saying the war would end on Tehran's terms, shortly after Iran said it had fired a volley of cruise missiles at a US aircraft carrier. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports. Iran rejects US peace plan, issues its own demands 25/03/2026 Middle East Israel's defence network challenged by Iranian cluster ballistic missiles 25/03/2026 Middle East Heritage sites in the Middle East under threat due to conflict 25/03/2026 Middle East Iran 'dismisses' US 15-point peace plan, issues its own ceasefire proposal 25/03/2026 Middle East Once seeking de-escalation, Saudi Arabia now sees ‘no coexistence’ with hardline Iran 25/03/2026 Middle East US goals shift: 'At the beginning of the Iran war, the US and Israel were on the same page' 25/03/2026 Middle East US demands of 15-point peace plan likely 'unacceptable' for Iran 25/03/2026 Middle East Unclear 'how much of a negotiation is taking place' between US and Iran 25/03/2026 Middle East What do we know of the US's 15-point peace plan sent to Iran? 25/03/2026 Middle East"
